UPDATE companies SET description='Wisconsin Metal Parts operates from Waukesha, Wisconsin. The company was founded in 1988 as Die Concepts, Inc., and spent its first 22 years building a tool-and-die business while listening to customer needs. In 2010 it rebranded to Wisconsin Metal Parts to reflect a broader service portfolio, and in 2024 it was acquired by SOLV Metals to join a larger group of metal manufacturers. Ownership and management have remained consistent through the transitions.

The shop provides full-service metal manufacturing under one roof, including CNC machining (turning, milling, drilling, tapping, boring, grinding), sheet metal fabrication (fiber laser cutting, CNC punching, bending, forming, welding, hardware insertion), custom metal stamping (progressive die, prototype to production), wire EDM (up to 16″ thick in conductive materials, including carbide), and tool-and-die design and build using simulation software. It runs nearly 60 million stampings per year at a 98% on-time delivery rate from two facilities in the Waukesha area.

Customers span aerospace, agriculture, foodservice, medical, and defense sectors. The company has produced military ordnance components such as mechanical fuzes, high-volume progressive die stampings for the container industry, and assemblies ranging from cabinets to clamping fixtures. It also supports commercial and industrial clients nationwide.

Wisconsin Metal Parts emphasizes intellectual value and a “Golden Rule” culture—treating customers, employees, and suppliers with respect. Its cross-trained workforce moves between departments to maintain workflow, and in-house tooling capabilities allow it to take over existing stamping dies and manage complex, multi-process parts from prototype through assembly.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR Registered','UL 580A Certified','NIST SP800-171 Compliant','Mil-Spec','RoHS','DFARS','REACH Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining (turning, milling, drilling, tapping, boring, grinding)", "Sheet metal fabrication (fiber laser cutting, CNC punching, bending, forming, welding, hardware insertion)", "Custom metal stamping (progressive die, prototype to production)", "Wire EDM (up to 16\u2033 thick, carbide cutting, 24/7 operation)", "Tool and die making (design, build, simulation software)", "Contract manufacturing and assembly (sub-assembly, full assembly)", "Stamping takeovers (existing die debug and run)", "Prototyping and reverse engineering", "CNC surface and form grinding", "Automatic hardware insertion tooling", "Quality inspection (CMM, optical comparators, vision systems, custom fixtures)", "Fiber laser cutting services", "Military fabrications (ordnance, fuze components)", "Shell casing machining", "Precision metal fabrication"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Agriculture", "Foodservice", "Medical", "Military/Defense", "Container industry", "General industrial"], "materials": ["Electrically conductive materials", "Tool steels", "Carbide", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Coordinate Measuring Machines (CMM)", "Optical comparators", "Height gauges and surface plates", "Vision inspection systems", "Custom inspection fixtures (built in-house)", "Keyence IM-7030", "Smart Scope Vision System (270x)", "Brown & Sharpe CNC 4-axis CMM", "Brown & Sharpe manual CMM", "Romer Arm CMM", "OGP Optical Comparators", "Leica Microscopes", "Computerized Linear Height Gage", "Virtek laser inspection system", "Force Gages", "Hardness Testers", "Hipot Testers", "Force Gauges", "Inspection Gages", "Assembly Simulation", "Fit and Function Gages", "Pressure Testing", "Leak Testing"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production; nearly 60 million stampings annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool and die design and build with forming/stamping simulation software", "Cross-trained employees deployed across departments to maintain workflow", "Nearly 60 million stampings per year at 98% on-time delivery", "Integrated fabrication, machining, stamping, and assembly under one roof", "ITAR registered and ISO 9001:2015 certified for defense and aerospace work"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 as Die Concepts, Inc. -> /about", "Acquired by SOLV Metals in 2024 -> /about", "Headquarters in Waukesha, Wisconsin -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "ITAR registered -> /quality", "UL 580A certified -> /quality", "NIST SP800-171 compliant -> /quality", "Nearly 60 million stampings per year at 98% on-time delivery -> /", "Serves aerospace, agriculture, foodservice, medical, military/defense -> /, /about", "CAGE code 1WSJ0 -> /quality", "Wire EDM up to 16\" thick, carbide cutting -> /", "CNC turning up to 3\" bar feed, 25.6\" swing, 40\" long -> /", "In-house tool and die design with simulation software -> /", "Cross-trained employees -> /about", "Integrated manufacturing under one roof -> /", "Fiber laser cutting, CNC punching, bending, forming, welding, hardware insertion, assembly -> /", "Inspection equipment: CMM, optical comparators, Keyence IM-7030, etc. -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We offer a variety of high-quality services including: CNC Machining, Sheet Metal Fabricating, Metal Stamping, Tool and Die Making, and partial and full Assembly services.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": ""