UPDATE companies SET description='Wood Components & Technologies operates from Cedar Falls, Iowa. The company''s history notes a shift toward manufacturing wood OEM parts for various industries, after earlier production of wood bearings for agricultural equipment and washing machines. No founding year or founder names are publicly disclosed.

The shop produces curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, and specialty millwork for commercial contractors and home builders, as well as wood and plastic OEM components for machinery equipment manufacturers. Core processes include CNC machining, arched and curved millwork, and lineal millwork. The facility also turns out custom arch windows, custom doors, and machined handrails. Headcount, facility size, and annual volume are not published.

Customers span commercial construction (architects, building centers, contractors, homeowners) and industrial OEMs in machinery, agriculture, and appliance sectors. A featured project for Jokers Comedy Club in Cedar Falls included custom arch windows, custom doors, and machined handrail.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Curved and arched moldings", "Lineal trim", "Specialty millwork", "Wood OEM parts", "Plastic OEM parts", "CNC machining", "Arched and curved millwork", "Lineal millwork", "Custom arch windows", "Custom doors", "Machined handrail", "Additional services", "Outside services"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Home building", "Machinery equipment manufacturing", "Agricultural equipment", "Washing machine manufacturing", "Architects", "Building centers", "Contractors", "Homeowners"], "materials": ["Wood", "Plastic"], "equipment": ["CNC"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom arched and curved millwork", "CNC machining for wood and plastic OEM parts", "Serves both commercial construction and industrial machinery OEMs", "Produces custom arch windows, doors, and handrails"], "facts_used": ["Location: Cedar Falls, Iowa -> /", "Products: curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, specialty millwork, wood and plastic OEM parts -> /", "Processes: CNC machining, arched & curved millwork, lineal millwork -> /", "Industries served: commercial contractors, home builders, machinery equipment manufacturers, agriculture equipment, washing machines -> /, db", "Example project: Jokers Comedy Club custom arch windows, doors, machined handrail -> /", "Equipment: CNC -> /", "Materials: wood, plastic -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /", "No founding year, ownership, founders, certifications, employee count, volume, lead time, tolerances, cage code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links found -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wood Components offers quality curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, and specialty millwork for commercial contractors and home builders, plus wood and plastic OEM parts and components for manufacturers of machinery equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wood-components-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Woods operates from Grand Forks, North Dakota, where it was founded in 1982 by Lowell and Georgia Innes. The business traces its roots to 1979, when Wood Products Inc. began as a cabinet shop serving Innes Construction, the founders'' home-building company. As commercial projects grew, the shop expanded its capabilities, and in 1982 American Woods was launched to meet customer demand for hardwood accessories. The two entities merged under the American Woods name in 2003, combining custom cabinetry and accessory lines under one roof.

The company runs a furniture manufacturing facility of approximately 160,000 square feet staffed by a 100-person team. Production covers the full sequence from milling, machining, sanding and sawing through sub-assembly, finishing and final assembly. Daily truck shipments move finished goods to distribution points nationwide. The operation is equipped to produce a wide range of home furnishing products, including indoor and outdoor collections, using real hardwoods and other premium materials.

American Woods supplies finished furniture to multiple nationally recognized brands. A long-standing partnership with Room & Board dates to 2001 and includes the Berkeley, Copenhagen and Danbury lines. Earlier, the workshop produced cedar outdoor pieces for major retailers such as Target, Costco and Lowe''s. The customer base consists primarily of resellers and national brands seeking American-made, high-end furniture for retail distribution.

The founders'' original vision — to craft timeless, quality, real wood products made in America and built to last — remains the stated mission. The company emphasizes craftsmanship, consistency and efficiency across every production stage, attributing its differentiation to the dedication of its team and a culture where integrity and pride guide each step.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Milling", "Machining", "Sanding and sawing", "Sub-assembly", "Finishing", "Final assembly", "Furniture manufacturing", "Cabinetry", "Outdoor furniture production", "Luxury furniture production"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Home furnishings", "Luxury furniture", "Retail furniture", "Contract furniture"], "materials": ["Real hardwoods", "Premium materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made furniture built to last", "Daily truck shipments for consistent nationwide delivery", "160,000 sq ft manufacturing facility with full in-house production", "100-person team covering milling through final assembly", "Long-term partnerships with national brands including Room & Board, Target, Costco and Lowe''s"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Lowell and Georgia Innes in Grand Forks, ND -> /about-us", "Wood Products Inc. started 1979 as cabinet shop for Innes Construction -> /about-us", "American Woods launched 1982 for hardwood accessories -> /about-us", "Merged under American Woods name 2003 -> /about-us", "Room & Board partnership began 2001 (Sherwood, Copenhagen, Danbury lines) -> /about-us", "Outdoor furniture for Target, Costco, Lowe''s in 1990s -> /about-us", "160,000 sq ft manufacturing facility -> /about-us", "100-person team -> /about-us", "Processes: milling, machining, sanding and sawing, sub-assembly, finishing, final assembly -> /about-us", "Daily truck shipments -> /about-us", "Materials: real hardwoods and other premium materials -> /about-us", "Supplies multiple nationally recognized brands -> /about-us", "Family-owned (same ownership since founding) -> /about-us", "Leadership team listed (Zach H., Tony C., Val A., Jeri I., Darrell H., Aaron E., Ashly K.) -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our furniture manufacturing facility spans approximately 160,000 square feet and is equipped to produce a wide range of high-quality home furnishing products.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wood-products-inc-dba-american-woods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
