g, real estate, fine art, photography, schools, breweries -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We could produce unique, customizable products that could still be mass produced.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodtech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company was founded in 1996 as a family-owned woodworking shop, built on a passion for transforming raw lumber into functional works of art.

The shop produces custom architectural woodwork, including entry doors, staircases with balusters, and precision-engineered wood veneers. It also offers shop milling services for contractors and designers. Projects move from concept to completion using CAD software for design, followed by hand fabrication and a final inspection step. The facility handles a range of wood species, though specific equipment and headcount are not disclosed.

The customer base spans homeowners, general contractors, and interior designers throughout the Los Angeles area.

The founders framed the venture as an art form rather than a trade, emphasizing craftsmanship, precision, and quality as guiding principles. The company positions its work as a blend of traditional hand skills and modern design tools, aiming to deliver timeless pieces that reflect the unique character of each wood species.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shop Milling Services", "Custom Door Fabrication", "Staircase and Baluster Fabrication", "Wood Veneer Engineering", "CAD Design", "Custom Wood Fabrication", "Quality Inspection"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Wood (various species)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db", "Headquarters in Pacoima, California -> db", "Family-owned -> /about", "Custom doors, stairs & balusters, veneer engineering -> /", "Shop milling services -> db, /", "CAD software used for design -> /", "Serves homeowners, contractors, designers -> /about", "Works with all types of woods -> /about", "Contacts: Anthony Aguirre, Leo Aguinaga, Antonio Aguirre -> /", "Principles: Craftsmanship, Precision, Quality -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Based in Los Angeles, CA, we are a family-owned Woodworking Shop that is dedicated to crafting custom handmade woodworks for our customers.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodworking-masters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Woodworks Distilling Co. operates from a facility in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The company was founded by Dave Wood and David Alexander to continue the craft-distilling tradition of small batches, local ingredients, and artisanal attention. Wood serves as founder and CEO, drawing on a background in retail, warehousing, and distribution, while Alexander serves as distiller, bringing expertise in chemistry, regulatory compliance, and cocktail design.

The distillery produces a range of spirits including corn-based vodka distilled six times, a four-grain vodka, dry and barrel-aged gins, bourbon and rye whiskeys sourced through its Preface Series, and an apple-pie corn liquor under the partner brand Horns Down Fine Spirits. Liqueurs such as Encheva and Nocino are in development.

The Horns Down partnership extends the portfolio into sports-oriented occasions. The company also hosts weddings, corporate events, and chef dinners, managed by front-of-house manager Abbey Elliot, who has nine years of beverage-industry experience.

The founders state that wood influences every facet of production, literally and figuratively, so that each spirit tells a distinct story. They launched the business to write the next chapter in craft distilling, aiming to earn the trial and ongoing support of drinkers who seek distinctive flavors and provenance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Distilling", "Barrel aging", "Blending", "Bottling", "Cocktail development", "Event hosting", "Product sourcing"], "industries": ["Craft distilling", "Spirits manufacturing", "Beverage alcohol", "Hospitality and events"], "materials": ["Corn", "Grains", "Botanicals", "Oak barrels", "Apples"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Small-batch, artisanal production with local ingredients", "Wood-influenced aging and flavor development", "Distiller-led recipe development and regulatory expertise", "On-site event space for private and community gatherings", "Partnership with Horns Down Fine Spirits for expanded portfolio"], "facts_used": ["Location: 912 W Britton Rd, Oklahoma City, OK 73114 -> /", "Founders: Dave Wood (Founder & CEO) and David Alexander (Distiller) -> /about", "Products: vodka (6x distilled corn, four-grain), gin (dry, western, barrel-aged), whiskey (bourbon, rye), apple pie corn liquor, liqueurs in development -> /", "Processes: distilling, barrel aging, blending, bottling -> /about, /", "Event space and hospitality services -> /, /about", "Front-of-house manager Abbey Elliot with 9 years experience -> /about", "Partnership with Horns Down Fine Spirits -> /", "Wood influences every facet of production -> /about", "Direct-to-consumer and distribution to bars/restaurants/retailers in Oklahoma -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "David Alexander Distiller Chemist. Regulatory guru. Cocktail designer. David brings a heady mix of science, legal savvy and damn good taste to his position as disti