UPDATE companies SET description='World Finer Foods, Inc. is headquartered in Bloomfield, New Jersey. The company traces its roots to 1947 when German immigrant Max H. Ries founded Reese Finer Foods after arriving in the United States in 1939. Originally intending to establish a textile business in Chicago, Ries pivoted to importing specialty foods, and the Reese brand quickly became a name in the U.S. specialty food market.

Today, World Finer Foods manages and markets more than 1,000 owned and third‑party premium food, beverage, and personal‑care products across over 60 brands. The firm provides a full suite of services — sales and category management, trade and consumer marketing, finance (order processing, invoicing, promotional spend, deductions, collections), and logistics (EDI, FDA compliance, inventory control, warehousing) — all supported by an Oracle ERP platform. It acts as the exclusive U.S. customer for its brand partners, selling to more than 350 retail and distribution accounts.

The company serves brand owners in the specialty food, beverage, and personal‑care sectors, including both domestic and international producers. Its portfolio includes long‑standing brands such as Reese (the top‑selling U.S. brand for artichoke hearts, hearts of palm, and prepared horseradish), Kitchens of India, Barry’s Tea, Nando’s, DaVinci, and La Posada. Customers range from traditional grocery retailers and distributors to emerging e‑commerce channels.

World Finer Foods emphasizes relationship‑driven growth, a philosophy dating to its early partnerships with European brands like Panni, Knorr, and Maggi. It is the only U.S. member of the Circle of European Specialty Food Distributors (CEISA) and a member of the Specialty Food Association and The Food Institute. The firm’s comprehensive approach — combining sales, marketing, finance, and logistics under one roof — is designed to let brand owners focus on product development while World Finer Foods handles market access.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Brand management", "Sales and category management", "Trade and consumer marketing", "Finance and order processing", "Logistics and warehousing", "EDI capability", "FDA compliance", "Inventory control", "Import and distribution", "E-commerce channel management", "Promotional spend processing", "Deduction processing", "Collections", "Oracle ERP system", "Relationship management with distributors and retailers"], "industries": ["Specialty foods", "Beverages", "Personal care", "Grocery retail", "Food distribution", "E-commerce", "Consumer packaged goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only U.S. member of the Circle of European Specialty Food Distributors (CEISA)", "Exclusive U.S. customer for brand partners, selling to 350+ retail and distribution accounts", "Comprehensive in\u2011house sales, marketing, finance, and logistics teams on a single Oracle ERP platform", "Reese brand holds #1 U.S. market position for artichoke hearts, hearts of palm, and prepared horseradish", "Decades\u2011long relationships with distributors and retailers across traditional and e\u2011commerce channels"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1947 by Max H. Ries as Reese Finer Foods -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Bloomfield, New Jersey -> db", "Manages and markets over 1,000 owned and third-party products across 60+ brands -> /about-us", "Provides sales, 