UPDATE companies SET description='Wyoming Welding & Machine LLC operates from Sheridan, Wyoming. The company was founded by Daniel Johlman, who started the business out of a desire to build a wider variety of challenging projects.

The shop provides contract manufacturing and metal fabrication services including laser cutting, forming, machining, welding, painting, and assembly. A Trumpf fiber laser handles cutting up to 1 inch mild steel, 3/4 inch stainless, 5/8 inch aluminum, and 3/8 inch titanium, copper, and brass. The company also fabricates structural steel packages for commercial and residential projects and works with design firms on architectural metalwork. Titanium is noted as a specialty, with thousands of pounds processed annually.

Customers span chemical, marine, energy, construction, aerospace, and industrial product sectors, along with general contractors and architectural/engineering firms in Wyoming and Montana. The firm delivers turnkey solutions from cut parts to complete welded and painted assemblies.

Johlman states the company was built to serve customers better than they have been served, guided by core values and a quality management system. The team emphasizes titanium expertise, turnkey capability, and access to state-of-the-art equipment either in-house or through subcontractors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract manufacturing", "Laser cutting (fiber laser)", "Metal forming", "CNC machining", "Welding", "Titanium and exotic metal fabrication", "Architectural metal fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "Structural steel erection", "Design and production integration", "Painting", "Assembly", "R&D to production"], "industries": ["Chemical", "Marine", "Energy", "Construction", "Aerospace", "Industrial products", "Architectural", "Structural steel (commercial and residential)"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Titanium", "Copper", "Brass"], "equipment": ["Trumpf fiber laser"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Titanium specialty with thousands of pounds processed per year", "Turnkey cutting, forming, welding, painting, and assembly", "Trumpf fiber laser with capacity up to 1\" mild steel, 3/4\" stainless, 5/8\" aluminum, 3/8\" titanium/copper/brass", "Collaboration with leading Wyoming and Montana design and engineering firms", "State-of-the-art equipment in-house and via subcontractors"], "facts_used": ["Location: Sheridan, Wyoming -> db", "Founder: Daniel Johlman -> /", "Founding motivation: love to build and challenging projects -> /", "Services: contract manufacturing, laser cutting, forming, machining, welding, painting, assembly -> /", "Equipment: Trumpf fiber laser -> /", "Laser cutting capacities: up to 1\" mild steel, 3/4\" stainless, 5/8\" aluminum, 3/8\" titanium/copper/brass -> /", "Titanium specialty: thousands of pounds per year -> /", "Industries: chemical, marine, energy, construction, aerospace, industrial products, architectural, structural steel -> / and db", "Customer types: general contractors, design/architectural/engineering firms in Wyoming and Montana -> /", "Turnkey solutions: cutting, forming, welding, painting, assembly -> /", "Quality management system and core values mentioned -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We take pride in building your product. We have many customers who trust us to build the products that they stake their reputation on", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wyoming-welding-machine-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='X-L Plastics Inc operates from Clifton, New Jersey, where it produces polyethylene film and bags for packaging applications. The company employs approximately 175 people at its facility on Clifton Boulevard, serving customers with an array of standard sizes and the capability to manufacture products to exact specifications.

The company manufactures a range of packaging materials including carton and drum liners, textile coverings, mattress bags, Gaylord and box liners, and bakery bags. Its core process is the extrusion of polyethylene film, which is converted into both vented and non-vented coverings. Custom designs are produced to exact customer specifications, with the sales team translating measurements into finished liners and coverings.

X-L Plastics serves the bakery, industrial, and janitorial sectors. Its bakery bags are designed to preserve freshness, while its industrial and janitorial bags are built for heavy-duty use. The company also supplies textile coverings and drum liners for broader packaging needs.

The company emphasizes environmental responsibility, encouraging recycling and waste reduction in its operations. It differentiates itself through its ability to tailor products to precise dimensions and its stock of various sizes for immediate needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion of polyethylene film and bags", "Custom design of liners and coverings", "Vented and non-vented material production", "Recycling programs", "Packaging material manufacturing", "Gaylord and box liner fabrication"], "industries": ["Bakery", "Industrial", "Janitorial"], "materials": ["Polyethylene"], "equipment": ["Polyethylene film extruders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom manufacturing to exact specifications", "Vented and non-vented material options", "Recycling and waste reduction initiatives", "Broad range of standard sizes in stock"], "facts_used": ["Location: Clifton, NJ -> page ''/''", "Employee count: 175 -> db", "Products: carton & drum liners, textile coverings, mattress bags, Gaylord and box liners, bakery bags -> page ''/''", "Process: extrusion of polyethylene film & bags -> page ''/''", "Custom design for Gaylord and box liners -> page ''/''", "Vented and non-vented materials available -> page ''/''", "Recycling and waste reduction focus -> page ''/''", "Industries served: bakery, industrial, janitorial -> industries_served", "Materials: polyethylene -> page ''/''", "Company type: manufacturer -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "X-L Plastics offers an array of sizes to accommodate our customers, as well as the capability to manufacture products to exact specifications.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "175", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='x-l-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Y.C. Cable was founded in Taiwan in 1985 as a specialist in monitor cables. The company entered the U.S. OEM market in 1991 and established Y.C. Cable USA Inc. in Fremont, California, in 1997. Today it operates from Fremont with additional sites in Irvine, Piscataway, New Taipei City, and Dongguan.

The company produces custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses for OEM applications, supporting prototype, new product introduction (NPI), build-to-print, and repeat production. Manufacturing processes include wire cutting, stripping, crimping, solder termination, connector assembly, harness assembly, shielding, overmolding, labeling, and electrical testing. Programs range from quick-turn prototypes to high-volume runs.

Y.C. Cable serves OEMs in AI and data centers, automation and robotics, medical, automotive, consumer electronics, industrial, and telecom/communications. Applications include automotive sensor and infotainment harnesses, medical diagnostic and monitoring equipment cables, consumer USB Type-C and Lightning assemblies, high-flex robotics cables, and high-density power and signal assemblies for GPU servers.

The company emphasizes its NPI process that bridges prototype to production, engineering support including DFM review and component sourcing, and a global footprint allowing flexible manufacturing location selection per program. It highlights 40-plus years of OEM experience and certifications across locations including ISO 9001, ISO 13485, and IATF 16949.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','ISO 45001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable cutting", "Stripping and preparation", "Crimping", "Solder termination", "Connector assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Shield preparation and termination", "Protective sleeving", "Heat-shrink application", "Overmolding", "Molded strain relief", "Labeling and identification", "Electrical testing", "Pinout verification", "Visual inspection", "Dimensional inspection", "Customer-defined testing", "Engineering design review & DFM", "BOM integration & project planning", "Component sourcing and line allocation", "Prototype & NPI builds", "Build-to-print manufacturing", "Contract wire harness manufacturing"], "industries": ["AI & Data Centers", "Automation & Robotics", "Medical", "Automotive", "Consumer Electronics", "Industrial", "Telecom & Communications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick-turn prototype and NPI builds", "Engineering and DFM support for manufacturability", "Global manufacturing footprint (US, Taiwan, China)", "Certifications including ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949", "Build-to-print and contract manufacturing services"], "facts_used": ["Founded in Taiwan in 1985 -> /about", "Entered US OEM market in 1991 -> /about", "Established Y.C. Cable USA Inc. in Fremont, California in 1997 -> /about", "Current operations in Fremont, Irvine, Piscataway, New Taipei City, Dongguan -> /about", "Manufactures custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses for OEM applications -> /", "Supports prototype, NPI, build-to-print, repeat production -> /", "Processes: wire cutting, stripping, crimping, solder termination, connector assembly, harness assembly, shielding, overmolding, labeling, electrical testing -> /about", "Industries served: AI & Data Centers, Automation & Robotics, Medical, Automotive, Consumer Electronics, Industrial, Telecom & Communications -> /about", "Applications: automotive sensor/infotainment harnesses, medical diagnostic/monitoring cables, consumer USB Type-C/Lightning, high-flex robotics cables, high-density GPU server assemblies -> /about", "NPI process bridges prototype to production -> /", "Engineering support includes DFM review, component sourcing -> /", "Certifications across locations: ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 45001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949 -> /about", "Global footprint allows flexible manufacturing location selection -> /about", "40+ years of OEM experience -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Y.C. Cable manufactures custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses for OEM applications", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='y-c-cable-yc-cable-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='YMI Industries operates from Grand Forks, North Dakota, where it has been a family-owned business since its founding in 1947. The company began as a specialist in tool and die components for metalworking, establishing a reputation for precision in that niche.

Today, YMI provides a broad range of metal fabrication and machining services, including laser cutting, metal stamping, CNC press brake bending, tool and die design and repair, welding and fabrication, CNC turning, CNC milling, and rapid prototyping. The shop runs multiple CNC press brakes, CNC lathes, and milling centers, and performs heat treating in-house. Metal stamping is offered for high-volume production, while prototyping services support low-volume and concept validation.

The company serves original equipment manufacturers, innovators, and industrial organizations across the metalworking sector. Customers rely on YMI for custom metal components, tooling, and fabricated assemblies, with the firm positioning itself as a one-stop shop through partnerships that extend into design, engineering, and finishing.

YMI’s guiding principle, “Making Response to Customers a Top Priority Since 1947,” underscores its focus on communication, accommodation, and competitive pricing. The ISO 9001-certified quality system employs coordinate measuring machines, go/no-go gauges, and in-process inspections to meet customer specifications, and the company commits to resolving non-conformities promptly.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Metal stamping", "Press brake bending (CNC)", "Tool and die design, production, and repair", "Welding and fabrication", "CNC turning", "CNC machining (milling)", "Heat treating (in-house)", "Rapid prototyping", "Custom design, engineering, and finishing (via partners)"], "industries": ["Metalworking", "OEM manufacturing", "Industrial manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC press brakes", "CNC lathes", "CNC milling machines", "Laser cutting machines", "Coordinate measuring machines (CMM)", "Go/no-go gauges"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1947 with a focus on customer response", "ISO 9001 certified quality management system", "In-house heat treating and a full range of CNC machining, stamping, and fabrication", "Rapid prototyping and one-stop-shop capabilities through partner network", "Wide tooling inventory on multiple CNC press brakes for high-tolerance bending"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1947 -> db", "Headquarters Grand Forks, North Dakota -> db", "Family-owned since 1947 -> /about", "ISO 9001 certified -> db and /quality", "Services: laser cutting, metal stamping, press brake bending, tool & die, welding & fabrication, turning machining, CNC machining, prototyping, custom services -> /services", "Equipment: CNC press brakes, CNC lathes, CNC milling machines, laser cutting machines, CMM, go/no-go gauges -> /services and /quality", "Industries: OEM manufacturers, innovators, organizations, metalworking -> /about", "Motto: Making Response to