UPDATE companies SET description='Zero Manufacturing is headquartered in North Salt Lake, Utah, and traces its founding to 1931 when German immigrant Herman Zierold established a sheet-metal shop in Los Angeles after crafting a rugged aluminum case to protect his engineering documents in the California oil fields. The business evolved through several ownership changes and was acquired by private equity firm Rockwood Equity Partners, with Declan Mclaughlin serving as CEO.

The company designs and manufactures protective cases and enclosures for mission-critical equipment, working in both aluminum and plastic. Its 286,000-square-foot facility employs 145 people and runs processes that include deep-drawn aluminum forming, rotomolding, laser cutting, Trumpf TruPunch pressing, certified welding, anodizing, powder coating, and custom assembly. Annual output exceeds 270,000 parts across more than 2,600 unique SKUs for a customer base of over 3,100 accounts.

Zero serves aerospace, defense, military, medical, energy, oil and gas, industrial, electronics and infrastructure, and logistics sectors. Its cases have protected avionics and flight hardware, medical diagnostics and life-saving devices, downhole sensors in harsh oilfield environments, and notably the Apollo 11 moon rock containers.

The company was born from a need to shield valuable documents from extreme field conditions, and it states its purpose is to help teams protect what matters through disciplined engineering, controlled domestic manufacturing, and long-term partnership. It emphasizes a fully U.S.-based, vertically integrated production model and an engineering-led approach that includes design guidance at no cost.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','MIL-STD']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Deep drawn aluminum forming", "Rotomolding plastic", "Aluminum laser cutting", "Trumpf TruPunch press operation", "Certified welding", "Aluminum and metal anodizing", "Painting and powder coating", "Surface finishing", "Standard and custom assembly", "Tooling and forming", "Custom tooling design", "Precision machining"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Military", "Medical", "Energy", "Oil & Gas", "Industrial", "Electronics & Infrastructure", "Logistics"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "High-strength aluminum", "Advanced polymers", "Rotomolded plastic"], "equipment": ["Trumpf TruPunch Press"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully domestic, vertically integrated manufacturing in a 286,000 sq ft facility", "Engineering-led design partnership offered at no cost", "Heritage includes Apollo 11 moon rock cases and decades of Mil-Spec work", "ISO 9001 certification with active military-related quality approvals", "Single-source capability for both deep-drawn aluminum and rotomolded plastic enclosures"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: North Salt Lake, Utah -> db", "Founded: 1931 -> db, homepage, /about-us", "Founder: Herman Zierold (German immigrant) -> /about-us", "Current ownership: Rockwood Equity Partners, CEO Declan Mclaughlin -> /about-us", "Employee count: 145 -> db, homepage", "Facility size: 286,000 sq ft -> homepage", "Annual parts produced: 270,000+ -> homepage", "Unique SKUs: 2,600 -> homepage", "Customer base: 3,100 -> homepage", "Processes: deep-drawn aluminum, rotomolding, laser cutting, Trumpf TruPunch, welding, anodizing, powder coating, assembly -> /capabilities, db", "Industries served: aerospace, defense, military, medical, energy, oil & gas, industrial, electronics & infrastructure, logistics -> /capabilities, db, homepage", "Apollo 11 moon rock cases -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certification -> db, /about-us", "MIL-STD and Mil-Spec approvals -> /about-us", "Materials: high-strength aluminum, advanced polymers, plastic -> homepage, /capabilities", "Engineering-led design partnership at no cost -> homepage", "Vertically controlled domestic production -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Great American manufacturer of custom cases. They make both plastic and aluminum, military grade, top of the line protection.", "founded_year": "1931", "employee_count": "145", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zero-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zell Manufacturing Company Inc. was founded in 1965 by Clifford R. Zell in Wilkinsburg, Pennsylvania. Shortly after, the business moved to its current location in Export, PA, about 25 miles east of Pittsburgh. The company remains family-owned, now operated by Clifford’s sons and grandchildren, preserving the original values of hard work and customer service.

The firm produces wooden and plastic components, custom moldings, and CNC-machined parts from a 9,000-square-foot facility equipped with fully automated machinery and custom molding equipment. Its capabilities span CNC machining, 5-cutter-head molding, gluing and clamping, panel fabrication, stair treads, countertops, and a range of finishing services including sanding, painting, staining, clear coating, silk screening, and wood burning. Assembly, packaging, and shipping are also handled in-house.

Zell serves industries such as construction, point-of-purchase advertising, furniture, consumer goods, architecture, interior design, manufacturing, and toy production. Its customer base includes both individual buyers and large corporations, with tailored solutions for each sector.

