UPDATE companies SET description='Zenith Electronics LLC is headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois. The company traces its origins to 1918, when it began with the advent of radio. Since 1999, it has operated as a wholly owned subsidiary of LG Electronics, serving as the South Korean conglomerate''s U.S. research arm.

Today Zenith functions as a technology development and licensing organization. Its work spans consumer electronics, hospitality, health care technologies, and broadcasting standards. The company created Pro:Idiom, an encryption technology widely adopted in the hospitality industry for delivering digital television signals, and administers licensing agreements that include royalty-free terms for qualified partners.

A concrete example is the deployment of Pro:Idiom by hotels and other hospitality venues to secure digital TV content distribution.

The company emphasizes a heritage of innovation dating back to its founding. Zenith inventors claim a series of industry firsts: the first wireless TV remote control, the first portable and push-button radios, the first stereo audio systems for FM radio and television, and the first terrestrial broadcast system for HDTV using digital technology.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Technology development", "Licensing", "Research and development", "Encryption technology (Pro:Idiom)", "Broadcasting standards development", "Hotel Internet Services"], "industries": ["Consumer electronics", "Hospitality", "Health care", "Broadcasting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pro:Idiom encryption technology for hospitality digital TV", "Royalty-free licensing for qualified companies", "LG Electronics'' U.S. research subsidiary since 1999", "Heritage of firsts: wireless TV remote, portable radio, HDTV broadcast system"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1918 -> db", "Headquarters Lincolnshire, Illinois -> db", "Wholly owned subsidiary of LG Electronics since 1999 -> db", "Technology development and licensing company -> db", "Created Pro:Idiom encryption technology -> /", "Pro:Idiom used in hospitality for digital TV signals -> /", "Heritage of innovation since 1918 -> /", "First wireless TV remote, portable radio, HDTV broadcast system -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Zenith Electronics LLC a leading U.S. technology development and licensing company.", "founded_year": "1918", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zenith-electronics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zenith Systems is headquartered in Bedford Heights, Ohio. The company traces its roots to the electrical construction industry, building a team of dedicated professionals with extensive capabilities in electrical, technology, audio/video, engineering, security, life safety, voice and data networking, and energy management systems.

The firm operates as a single-source provider for electrical and technology construction and design. Its service offerings span electrical construction, teledata and voice/data networking, audio/video system integration, security system integration, fire alarm and life safety systems, and full-service electrical engineering design. Zenith handles projects ranging from simple lighting installations to the design-build of electrical and technology infrastructure for half-million-square-foot healthcare facilities, emphasizing on-time, on-budget delivery.

Zenith serves a diverse client base across healthcare, education, industrial, energy and renewables, data centers, transportation, government, historic renovation, commercial, and utilities sectors. Notable projects include work at Tripoint Medical Center and the St. John Medical Center modernization. The company also supports industrial and commercial clients with 24/7/365 emergency service and ongoing maintenance.

The company differentiates itself through a quality management system embedded in every project phase, a combined security experience exceeding 200 years, and recognition as a top-50 audio/video integrator in the United States. Zenith’s founding mission centers on providing cost-effective, reliable solutions while continuously adopting technologies.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical construction", "Teledata/voice and data networking", "Audio/video system integration", "Security system integration", "Fire alarm and life safety systems", "Electrical engineering design", "Design-build project delivery", "Installation and commissioning", "24/7 emergency service", "Energy management systems"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Education", "Industrial", "Energy and Renewables", "Data Centers", "Transportation", "Government", "Historic Renovation", "Commercial", "Utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Bedford Heights, Ohio -> db", "Services: Electric, Teledata, Audio Video, Security, Fire Alarm, Engineering Design -> /", "Markets served: Healthcare, Education, Industrial, Energy and Renewables, Data Centers, Transportation, Government, Historic Renovation, Commercial, Utilities -> /", "24/7 emergency service -> /", "Quality management embedded in every phase -> /quality", "Recognized as top 50 audio/video integrator -> / (Audio Video section)", "Over 200 years combined security experience -> / (Security section)", "Projects: Tripoint Medical Center, St. John Medical Center Modernization -> db (industries_served)", "Company description: electrical and technology construction and design organization -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Zenith Systems is an electrical and technology construction and design organization, bringing decades of experience and expertise to projects of all sizes; from the installation of a simple lighting project to the design/build of the electrical and technology infrastructure of a half million square foot healthcare facility.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zenith-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ziroli Woodworking operates from Pāpa''aloa on the Big Island of Hawai''i. The business traces its roots to 1975, when Peter Ziroli opened his first shop in Honolulu. Today it remains a family-owned and operated woodshop, with Peter''s lifework and passion guiding every piece that leaves the bench.

The shop produces handmade custom furniture, architectural millwork, and cabinetry, collaborating closely with each client from concept through installation. Work is executed using a mix of heirloom hand tools — including chisels passed down from Peter''s father, Alfred — and modern production saws. Beyond fabrication, the company runs local woodworking workshops and apprenticeship programs, extending its craft into education.

Notable commissions have come from filmmaker Francis Ford Coppola, musician David Crosby, Paul Mitchell Systems, Adams Design, artist Irving Jenkins, and former Bank of Hawai''i CEO Larry Johnson. The shop also serves the broader community with in-person cabinetry and architectural installation services across the Big Island.

Ziroli Woodworking emphasizes locally sourced, ethically harvested Hawaiian hardwoods — primarily acacia koa, mango, and ''ōhi''a — often incorporating recycled material. The company states its differentiator is a cooperative, relationship-driven process that aims to deliver both a beloved object and an experience worth returning for.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Custom cabinetry", "Architectural millwork and installations", "Woodworking workshops and education", "Hand-tool and machine-based wood fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Architectural millwork", "High-end custom woodworking", "Interior design and build-outs"], "materials": ["Acacia koa", "Mango", "''\u014chi''a", "Recycled hardwoods", "Sustainably harvested hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1975", "Locally sourced, ethically harvested Hawaiian hardwoods (koa, mango, ''\u014dhi''a)", "Master woodworker lineage \u2014 Peter Ziroli trained by his father Alfred", "Custom collaboration process with each client", "Woodworking workshops and apprenticeship programs for the community"], "facts_used": ["Location: P\u0101pa''aloa, Hawaii -> db", "Founded 1975, first shop in Honolulu -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Founder Peter Ziroli, trained by father Alfred -> /about-us", "Custom furniture, cabinetry, architectural installations -> /about-us, /", "Woodworking workshops and apprenticeship programs -> /about-us, /", "Materials: acacia koa, mango, ''\u014dhi''a, recycled/sustainably harvested -> /about-us", "Tools: antique chisels, state-of-the-art saws -> /about-us", "Notable clients: Francis Ford Coppola, David Crosby, Paul Mitchell, Jack Adams, Irving Jenkins, Larry Johnson -> /about-us", "Serving community for over 40 years -> /", "In-person services on Big Island -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Whether it''s custom-made cabinets or a dining room table, we create pieces that are designed to withhold the test of time.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ziroli-woodworking-hawai-i-handmade-wood-furniture-and-cabinetry' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ZoRoCo Packaging was founded in 2007 in Caldwell, Idaho, by Cordy and Kim Rost. They acquired a small frozen food packaging business called IdaCold, and with the involvement of Kim''s father, food industry executive Marc Ikebasu, began building a contract manufacturing operation.

Today ZoRoCo operates three manufacturing facilities on a campus about 30 minutes southwest of Boise, employing over 400 people. The plants hold GFSI BRCGS A+ to AA ratings and specialize in frozen and allergen-free food contract manufacturing and co-packing. Capabilities include IQF processing of vegetables, fruits, and plant-based products; blending, enrobing, and chopping; vertical form-fill-seal bagging from 4 ounces to 6 pounds; tray and carton shrink wrapping; lidded tubs and peel-and-go cups; bulk packaging up to 60 pounds; and high-care ready-to-eat production in 20,000 square feet of expanded space added in 2019. A USDA-approved cold storage facility provides 4,500 temperature-controlled pallet positions with cross-docking, container loading, and export documentation services.

The company serves food brands and entrepreneurs across the frozen, gluten-free, allergen-free, and plant-based segments. Clients range from startups launching vegan cheese and butter spreads to established brands needing co-packing for IQF produce, ready-to-eat meals, and variety packs. ZoRoCo''s dedicated gluten-free plant (built 2022) and Big 9 allergen-free capabilities allow it to handle sensitive formulations without cross-contamination risk.

ZoRoCo positions itself as a non-competitor—it markets no brands of its own—and emphasizes transparency through live client access to production, inventory, and shipping data. The founders cite an entrepreneurial mentality, precision execution, and certification and claims management as core differentiators, aiming to protect clients'' intellectual property while scaling capacity alongside their growth.', certifications=ARRAY['BRCGS','GFSI BRCGS A+ rating','GFSI BRCGS AA rating','USDA-approved facility']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Frozen food contract manufacturing", "Co-packing services", "IQF processing (vegetables, fruits, plant-based)", "Blending and enrobing", "Chopping and dicing", "Vertical form-fill-seal (VFFS) bagging (4 oz\u20136 lb)", "Tray and carton shrink packaging", "Hand-packed tray packaging", "Lidded tubs and peel-and-go cups", "Bulk packaging (10\u201360 lb)", "Club pack, variety pack, bag-in-bag packaging", "Parent/child packaging configurations", "High-care ready-to-eat production", "Cold storage (4,500 temperature-controlled pallet positions)", "USDA-approved cold storage operations", "Container loading and cross-docking", "Export documentation and slip sheeting", "Order fulfillment and distribution", "Allergen-free manufacturing (Big 9 allergens)", "Gluten-free manufacturing", "Plant-based product manufacturing", "Vegan emulsion butter spreads and sticks production", "Vegan cheese production"], "industries": ["Food contract manufacturing", "Food co-packing", "Frozen foods", "Gluten-free foods", "Allergen-free foods", "Plant-based foods", "Ready-to-eat foods", "Private label food manufacturing"], "materials": ["Laminated packaging films", "Kraft paper", "Gusseted bags", "Steamable bags", "Sauce packet insertion materials"], "equipment": ["Vertical form-fill-seal (VFFS) machines", "IQF processing equipment", "High-care production rooms (insulated metal panels, coated flooring, HVAC)", "Refrigerated loading dock", "Cold storage racking 