UPDATE companies SET description='iSolar is based in St. Paul Park, Minnesota, and was co-founded in 2019 by master electrician John Ihle and his nephew Ryan Ihle. The company is family-owned and veteran-owned, with roots in the Minnesota electrical trade dating back to 1977 and renewable-energy work since the 1980s — experience the firm says few other solar installers in the state can match.

iSolar provides full-service solar, storage, and electrical work for homes, farms, and businesses across Minnesota. Its services cover residential solar, commercial and agricultural solar, battery backup, EV charger installation, electrical panel upgrades, wiring, standby generators, and solar array detach-and-reset for roofing projects. The company uses its own crew for installations, completing most residential jobs in one to two days under master electrician license EA761814. It holds manufacturer certifications for major brands including Enphase, SolarEdge, Tesla Powerwall, Generac, and Kohler, and backs every system with a 30-year insurance-backed warranty through Solar Insure plus a 20-year battery warranty.

The installer serves Minnesota homeowners, farmers, businesses, schools, and public entities. Since 2020 it has helped income-qualified families access solar at little-to-no cost through Xcel Energy''s Solar*Rewards Income-Qualified program. Since 2019 it has assisted farmers with projects funded partly by USDA REAP grants. Public-sector work includes solar on school buildings and a 100 kW AC array at Edina City Hall. iSolar has also been selected as a co-op installer by Solar United Neighbors for 2022, 2023, and 2024.

The company says it was started to do solar "the right way" for neighbors — emphasizing a single local crew from start to finish with no subcontractor shuffle, custom solutions from experienced designers, honest fair pricing, and a 30-year warranty. Its family-owned, veteran-owned structure and deep Minnesota roots are presented as reasons customers can trust the firm for the long term.', certifications=ARRAY['BBB A+ Accredited','NABCEP Certified','Solar Insure Certified Provider','QMerit Partner','Angi Certified Installer','Veteran-Owned','Family-Owned','Enphase Certified','SolarEdge Certified','APsystems Certified','Tigo Certified','Tesla Powerwall Certified','Enphase IQ Battery Certified','EG4 Certified','Sol-Ark Certified','HomeGrid Certified','Fortress Power Certified','Generac Certified','Kohler Certified','Minnesota Electrical License EA761814']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Agricultural solar installation", "Battery backup installation", "EV charger installation", "Electrical panel upgrades", "Electrical wiring", "Standby generator installation", "Solar array detach and reset", "Permitting and interconnection management", "System design and engineering", "30-year warranty administration"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Education", "Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Enphase inverters", "SolarEdge inverters", "APsystems", "Tigo", "Tesla Powerwall", "Enphase IQ Battery", "EG4", "Sol-Ark", "HomeGrid", "Fortress Power", "Generac generators", "Kohler generators", "Tesla EV chargers", "Enphase EV chargers", "ChargePoint EV chargers", "Wallbox EV chargers", "Emporia EV chargers", "Grizzl-E EV chargers", "Autel EV chargers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Interconnection 6-8 weeks; installation 1-2 days on site", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same local crew starts and finishes every job \u2014 no subcontractor shuffle", "First in Minnesota to offer So