UPDATE companies SET description='The company''s origins trace to the work of researchers including Christian Buess, whose doctoral thesis and subsequent publications laid the groundwork for transit-time ultrasonic flow measurement. Since its inception, ndd has focused on translating that technology into clinical pulmonary function testing.

The company designs and manufactures a line of portable spirometers and complete pulmonary function testing systems under the EasyOne brand. The portfolio includes the EasyOne Air and Sky for spirometry, the EasyOne Pro and Pro LAB for diffusion capacity (DLCO), lung volumes, and multi-breath washout (MBW), as well as the PC-based EasyOne on-PC and the integrated EasyOne Connect software platform. All devices employ ndd''s proprietary TrueFlow ultrasound technology, which eliminates the need for routine calibration, and TrueCheck self-quality-control routines.

ndd''s instruments are used in clinics, hospitals, and research institutions worldwide. The company cites deployments in clinical, veterinary, high-altitude, sea-level, and space environments. Its products have supported major research initiatives such as the World Trade Center health monitoring programs, the COPDGene study, the BOLD and PLATINO initiatives, and the MACS study, serving pulmonologists, primary-care physicians, and clinical researchers.

The company''s stated mission is to make early, accurate lung-disease detection the standard of care. It emphasizes that calibration-free operation, portability, and seamless EMR/EHR integration lower barriers to routine spirometry, enabling earlier diagnosis and better patient outcomes. HITRUST-certified cloud data management and centralized PFT review further differentiate the offering.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','HITRUST']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spirometry", "DLCO (diffusing capacity) testing", "Full pulmonary function testing (PFT)", "Multi-breath washout (MBW) testing", "Calibration-free ultrasound flow measurement", "TrueCheck self-quality control", "EMR/EHR integration", "Cloud-based data management (nddCloud)", "Centralized PFT review", "Initial in-service"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Pulmonary function testing", "Respiratory diagnostics", "Clinical research", "Veterinary medicine", "High-altitude physiology", "Space medicine"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["EasyOne Air", "EasyOne Sky", "EasyOne Pro", "EasyOne Pro LAB", "EasyOne on-PC", "EasyOne Connect", "TrueFlow ultrasound technology", "TrueCheck technology"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Calibration-free TrueFlow ultrasound flow measurement", "TrueCheck self-quality-control technology", "Portable, lightweight device design", "HITRUST-certified secure cloud data platform (nddCloud)", "Bi-directional integration with major EMR/EHR systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> /about", "Headquarters in Andover, Massachusetts -> db", "ISO 13485 certification -> db", "TrueFlow ultrasound technology developed from ETH Zurich research -> /about", "Product lines: EasyOne Air, Sky, Pro, Pro LAB, on-PC, Connect -> /", "Calibration-free operation and TrueCheck self-quality control -> /", "Used in clinical, veterinary, high-altitude, sea-level, space applications -> /about", "Research partnerships: World Trade Center health monitoring, COPDGene, BOLD