UPDATE companies SET description='1st Choice Millworks operates from Coeur d''Alene, Idaho, where it was founded in 2007 by Ted Yurek after he acquired woodworking equipment and began supplying custom mouldings to local building suppliers. The business remained a one-man operation for a decade until 2017, when his son Ryan Yurek joined, and the pair transitioned ownership in 2019 to focus on high-end architectural millwork for luxury home builders.

The shop produces custom architectural millwork, interior and exterior doors, siding, paneling, and specialty wood components, handling design, fabrication, pre-finishing, and installation under one roof. Its facility turns out nearly one million linear feet of lumber each year, supported by a nine-person team that includes a shop foreman, finish specialist, estimators, and operators.

The company serves super-premium home builders, architects, and developers in the Pacific Northwest, with projects such as the Black Rock development in Coeur d''Alene, where it pre-finished exterior cladding for a major luxury residence.

